<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        The BUY-SIDE PSA path, for the Acquisition_PSA record type.
        Four steps: Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready for Execution -> Executed.

        EVERY <info> TEXT BELOW IS COPIED BYTE-IDENTICAL FROM Contract_Review_Negotiation_Path,
        the __MASTER__ path this file supersedes (now deactivated, retained as the record of
        that text). Nothing on the acquisition side is reworded, re-ordered, added or dropped by
        this tranche. The absence of <fieldNames> on every step is ALSO carried forward
        deliberately - the master path declared none, and adding key fields here would change
        what an acquisition user sees on a live Path for no requested reason.

        ⚠ THE FIRST STEP CONTAINS `&amp;amp;amp;` AND THAT IS NOT A TYPO INTRODUCED HERE - it is
        the master path's own bytes, reproduced exactly. Whether it renders as an ampersand or
        as the literal text depends on how the Path component treats the stored string, which
        this repo has never confirmed. It is left alone on the byte-identical rule; if it is
        ever judged wrong it should be fixed as its own change, on both this file and the
        deactivated original, not silently while doing something else. The new disposition path
        sidesteps the question by using the word "and".

        ⚠ DRIVEN BY Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c - inherited from the master path and
        still the load-bearing reason this Path works. Stage__c is a DERIVED PROJECTION:
        Contract_Review_Stage_Sync recomputes it from Negotiation_Status__c on every save and a
        direct write to it commits and is silently discarded. 'Revised' and 'Ready for
        Execution' BOTH project to 'Review', so a Stage__c Path would sit still through one of
        the Advance Stage clicks. On Negotiation_Status__c the Path and the button are the SAME
        sequence.

        WHY A NEW FILE AT ALL. A Path is configured PER RECORD TYPE and recordTypeName cannot be
        re-pointed on an existing PathAssistant, so a __MASTER__ path cannot be adopted by a new
        record type. Same shape as Tranche 2's Disposition_Path split, 3A's NDA_Path split and
        3B's LOI_Path split.

        STEP ORDER COMES FROM THE PICKLIST, NOT FROM THIS FILE. Negotiation_Status__c is ordered
        Initial Draft, Revised, Ready for Execution, Executed (sorted=false), which is exactly
        the intended line. ⚠ UNLIKE LOI__c AND NDA__c THERE WAS NO ORDERING PROBLEM TO SOLVE
        HERE, because no value was added: both record types expose the SAME four values, so the
        two PSA paths render the same sequence and differ only in wording.

        =====================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-14 (Phase 3, observation 7). THE FOUR-STEP SEQUENCE AND THE
        "NO ORDERING PROBLEM" PARAGRAPH ARE BOTH SUPERSEDED. THERE WAS AN ORDERING PROBLEM AND
        IT WAS THE SHARPEST ONE IN THE PHASE.
        =====================================================================

        RETRACTED (1), verbatim: "Four steps: Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready for Execution ->
        Executed" and "EVERY <info> TEXT BELOW IS COPIED BYTE-IDENTICAL FROM
        Contract_Review_Negotiation_Path... Nothing on the acquisition side is reworded,
        re-ordered, added or dropped by this tranche."
        The target buy-side sequence is now Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed. Three
        values were added to Negotiation_Status__c for this record type alone. The
        byte-identical rule described Tranche 3C and was never a standing property; the three new
        <info> texts below are NEW PROSE.

        RETRACTED (2), verbatim: "UNLIKE LOI__c AND NDA__c THERE WAS NO ORDERING PROBLEM TO SOLVE
        HERE, because no value was added: both record types expose the SAME four values."
        🔴 THERE IS ONE NOW, AND IT IS WORSE THAN LOI__c's. The shared value is 'Executed' - the
        TERMINAL - and it already sat at position 4. Appending the three new values would have
        rendered THIS PATH as Executed, Draft, Negotiation, Signed: the finish line FIRST, on a
        Path that deploys green and passes every test. The three values were therefore INSERTED
        BEFORE 'Executed' in the master value set. See Negotiation_Status__c's own comment for
        the full arithmetic. ⚠ LOI__c.Stage__c in this same phase needed an APPEND and NDA__c
        needed an INTERLEAVE - three fields, three different answers. Redo the arithmetic every
        time; it does not transfer.

        ✅ P3-D3 DONE. The seven-step transitional state described above is retired. 'Initial
        Draft', 'Revised' and 'Ready for Execution' are removed from THIS FILE and from the
        Acquisition_PSA record type - and, per decision O3, they are NOT deactivated on the
        field, because Disposition_PSA still runs on all three. The four steps below are now the
        whole file: Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed. Applied via
        agent-output/p3-d3-retire-loi-psa/.

        ⚠ 'Signed' IS NOT 'Executed', AND THE PATH SAYS SO ON PURPOSE. 'Signed' is the analogue
        of the retired 'Ready for Execution' - the document is final and signatures are in hand -
        while 'Executed' remains the value that fires ContractExecutionService's handoff and
        stamps the Opportunity Contract Signed (Day 0). Contract_Review_Stage_Sync
        projects 'Signed' to the coarse Stage__c = 'Review', exactly as 'Ready for Execution'
        did, and ONLY 'Executed' projects to 'Contract Execution'. Do not "tidy" that by making
        'Signed' project to Contract Execution - it would move the handoff a step early.

        🔴 THE 'Executed' HOP DOES NOT CREATE THE Transaction__c, AND THIS FILE SAID IT DID.
        The sentence above ended "...and creates the Transaction" when first written in this
        pack. That phrasing has been FALSE SINCE 2026-08-05 and is marked FALSE in
        RecordStageAdvanceService's own map comment (search "used to say this hop"): creation
        moved to ContractExecutionService.openTransactionsOnAboutToClose, which keys on
        Opportunity.StageName = 'About to Close' - verified in that class, not carried from
        prose. The 'Executed' hop stamps the Day-0 DATE that the later creation READS BACK, so
        the two stay coupled; they simply no longer run in the same transaction.
        ⚠ THE CONCLUSION ABOVE IS UNAFFECTED - 'Signed' must still not project to
        'Contract Execution'. What changes is only WHAT the 'Executed' hop does, not whether it
        is the hop that matters.

        ⚠ THE SAME CLAIM WAS ALSO ON SCREEN, IN THE 'Executed' STEP'S <info>, AND IT IS FIXED
        HERE - BUT IT WAS INHERITED, NOT INTRODUCED BY THIS PACK. That text arrived byte-identical
        from pathAssistants/Contract_Review_Negotiation_Path (the pre-record-type master path)
        when this file was split off, and it read "...the Transaction record is created
        automatically". It now reads "...the Transaction record itself is created later, when the
        deal reaches About to Close". This pack is simply the first thing to touch the file since
        the behaviour moved on 2026-08-05, which is why the correction lands here.
        🔴 THE MASTER PATH STILL CARRIES THE ORIGINAL WORDING - measured 2026-08-14, not assumed.
        It is PRE-EXISTING and deliberately OUT OF SCOPE for this pack; fix it as its own change
        so the diff stays reviewable. Contract_Review_Path_Disposition is unaffected: its
        'Executed' step describes the sale moving into Closing and never mentions a Transaction.

        POST-DEPLOY: this path renders nothing until every existing Contract Review row has been
        migrated off Master onto Acquisition_PSA and the record type is assigned in the profiles
        in use - the same gate Tranche 2's A2 established, for the same reason.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>Contract_Review__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Negotiation_Status__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Contract Review Path Acquisition</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Draft the purchase and sale agreement from the agreed LOI terms. Circulate the first draft and capture the PSA date.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Draft</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Negotiate the PSA. Validate terms, contingencies and timelines. Redlines happen here: log every exchange with Log Version — each one records who sent it and flips Ball In Court — and stay on this step for as long as the negotiation runs. Advance only once the document is final.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Negotiation</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Signed by both sides. The document is final and signatures are in hand, but the deal has not yet been handed to Transactions — advancing from here executes the contract, so confirm every contingency and date is agreed first.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Signed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>PSA fully executed — this hands the deal off to the Transactions team: the Opportunity is stamped Contract Signed (Day 0) and the execution date is stamped for you. The Transaction record itself is created later, when the deal reaches About to Close.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Executed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>Acquisition_PSA</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
